{
  "id": "neo-summer-road-2001",
  "name": "Neo Summer Road 2001",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "Pokémon Card Battle★Neo Summer Road was Japan's summer tournament circuit of 2001, in seven regions from Sapporo on 20 July to Fukuoka on 12 August 2001, with branding themed on Ho-Oh. The top three of each tournament won No. 1, No. 2 or No. 3 Trainer cards. Its trophy cards keep Ken Sugimori's art from 2000's World Challenge cards, in a boy's and a girl's version, with more Pokémon the higher the place, but their text names only the event, not the junior or senior division. Each winner's name, tournament, division and place were printed above the picture, and the card came in an acrylic trophy case. Spare copies with nothing printed above the picture, probably straight from the printer, have since turned up. The winners' list in Trainers magazine shows two girls among its 56 winners, both third-place finishers.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Pokumon: Pokémon Card Battle Neo Spring / Summer Road 2001",
        "url": "https://pokumon.com/pokemon-card-battle-neo-spring-summer-road-2001/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Pokumon: Girl Neo Summer No.3 Trainer (World Challenge Summer 2001)",
        "url": "https://pokumon.com/card/girl-neo-summer-no-3-trainer-world-challenge-summer-2001-unnumbered/"
      }
    ]
  },
